"""Flagship slice 2d.2: bypass attempts on OBAAF-JEN-009, untrusted text built into a command.

Each case is one attempt, run as a Jenkinsfile: 172 by an Opus 5.5 attacker that did not write the rule
(ids A001 to A172), on the rule as it was at `653b153`, and 29 by the run that took the slice (ids B-a01
to B-a30), before it changed anything. `expected` is what OBAAF-JEN-009 says after the slice
("finding-<severity>", "unknown" for cannot tell, or "quiet"); `before` is what it said at `653b153`
(recorded, not asserted); `why` is the attacker's judgement. LIMITS names the cases whose answer is a
stated limit: the answer judged right, and why the rule gives another. The record is
docs/bypass-attempts.md.
"""
import time
import unittest

